WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
- Charles Entertainment Cheese

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:03.900
was likely born sometime
in the early 1970s

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.500
in the northeast United States.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.660
We don't know exactly when
his date of birth was,

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:08.990
in fact, nobody does.

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:10.930
Because his parents passed
away when he was young

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:12.300
and his earliest recorded history

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.300
was when he was first moved

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.380
into St. Marinara's
orphanage as an infant.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.030
Charles resented being an orphan

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:19.410
because he never got to
celebrate his own birthday party.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:20.810
And to add insult to injury,

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:22.590
there were so many kids at this orphanage

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.310
that somebody's birthday was
being celebrated every week.

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:26.940
Despite the bubbling depression

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.660
building up under this forced smile,

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.850
the caretakers at the
orphanage apparently refused

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.170
to throw Charles a
celebration of any kind.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:34.310
It seems like it would've been easy

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:36.450
to just pick the day that he
showed up at the orphanage

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:37.283
and celebrate that,

00:00:37.283 --> 00:00:38.840
but I'm guessing that these people

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.920
had a cruel prejudice against rats.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:42.550
In fact, he seems to be the only rat

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:43.940
enrolled at the orphanage.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:46.100
Charles Entertainment, or
as he would become known

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.840
by his contemporaries, Chuck E,

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:49.900
was primarily interested in playing games

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:50.880
and making music.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:51.897
In a tragic twist of fate,

00:00:51.897 --> 00:00:54.820
one of his favorite songs
was "Happy Birthday."

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.000
He also had a third passion,
albeit a much less healthy one,

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.330
a passion for pizza.

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:00.163
In fact, it seems

00:01:00.163 --> 00:01:01.820
that this might have been
one of the only things

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:02.653
that kept him going

00:01:02.653 --> 00:01:04.570
through the countless
birthday parties of others

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:07.090
and cruel mistreatment by
the orphanage caretakers.

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:09.120
But despite Charles' optimistic mindset

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:10.800
during a bad situation in his youth,

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.610
his later years would break him down

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:15.270
as he would be hit with
bankruptcy, horrifying opponents,

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:16.950
potential drug and gambling problems,

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.410
public health conspiracies,
alleged predatory behavior,

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.450
more bankruptcy and identity
scandal, and much, much more

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:24.880
during his rise to power.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:29.060
- [Man] A powerful rat named
Charles Entertainment Cheese.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:29.940
- [Woman] Chuck E. Cheese

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.320
is filing for bankruptcy protection.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:35.050
- [Man] Losing over 28
million last year alone.

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:36.500
- [Man] The meth must be a hell of a drug.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.950
- There is something
wrong with Chuck E., guys.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:41.710
- [Man] They've reported losses
five of the last six years

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:42.930
since the acquisition.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:44.450
- [Man] Vomit, disinfectant.

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:45.809
- [Man] I got to experience it.

00:01:45.809 --> 00:01:48.160
I got to experience the truth.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:51.180
- So I have a theory that
I have wanted to talk about

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:52.104
for a long time.

00:01:52.104 --> 00:01:54.020
- [Man] Vomit disinfectant.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:55.680
- [Woman] There is in fact a sex den

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.480
in every Chuck E. Cheese.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.240
- That was like my first introduction

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.190
to the sound that you hear at the casino.

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:02.303
- [Man] He chuckled and responded,

00:02:02.303 --> 00:02:03.830
don't worry about that, bud,

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:05.290
this job is off the books.

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:07.447
- [Woman] Those are hand
prints on the window.

00:02:07.447 --> 00:02:12.447
♪ You just found ♪

00:02:13.247 --> 00:02:15.397
♪ The Chuck E. Cheese ♪

00:02:15.397 --> 00:02:17.634
(Chuck E. Cheese screams)

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:21.467
(dramatic metal music)

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:25.100
- Welcome to "Horror History."

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.020
I am your professor,

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.943
apparently a less
successful Macaulay Culkin.

00:02:27.943 --> 00:02:29.660
I mean, he is pretty successful.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:30.493
In today's lesson,

00:02:30.493 --> 00:02:32.470
I'll be analyzing the entire known history

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:34.650
of big pizza's most infamous mascot.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:37.010
Sorry Papa, it's rodent season.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:38.610
- He has no pizza experience.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:41.060
- Chuck is most known as the
musically inclined mammal

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.490
who serves as the figurehead
of CEC Entertainment's

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:48.120
primary cash cow or... cash rat?
Chuck E. Cheese Restaurants.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:51.230
So come on down for some rat
pizza at our child casino

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:53.190
and join me in covering the entire history

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.090
of Charles Entertainment Cheese.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:57.130
To fully understand the
whiskered wheeler dealer,

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:58.730
I'm gonna take it back to his childhood

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:00.599
at St. Marinara's orphanage.

00:03:00.599 --> 00:03:04.432
(dramatic suspenseful music)

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:08.230
Charles spent a lot of
time playing the game Pong

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:09.560
and became very good at it.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.630
So he decided to test his
skills in a tournaments,

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:14.040
where he won a trophy and $50 prize money.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.750
He used the money to pay for
a bus ticket to New York city.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:19.910
But it's not entirely clear to
me why a rat who at this time

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:21.500
was smaller than the size of a pizza

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.200
would need to pay to use the bus.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.020
He didn't really think
this trip through, I guess

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.870
because he had nowhere to
stay when he got there.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:28.460
So he slept above a pizza kitchen

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:30.080
because he was attracted to the smell.

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:32.860
It was there that he discovered
Pasqually P Pieplate,

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:35.590
an Italian pizza chef by
day and a drummer by night.

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:37.750
Pasqually loved to listen
to music while he worked.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.760
So being an aspiring musician himself,

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:41.250
Chuck E. felt right at home.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:45.100
That is until one
treacherous evening in 1977.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.760
After Pasqually went home for the night,

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.920
Charles liked to come down
and explore the kitchen

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:51.190
and making him very
similar to other media rats

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:54.080
like Remy from Ratatouille
or Chef Marcel Toing

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.503
from Ratatoing.

00:03:55.503 --> 00:04:00.503
(laughing) What are they doing?

00:04:02.788 --> 00:04:05.480
What is this, what is this?

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:08.780
Only on this occasion, Pasqually
had not actually left yet

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:10.350
and Charles was discovered.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.260
Mouse, screamed Pasqually,

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:13.710
incorrectly identifying him.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:15.030
Pasqually grabbed a rolling pin

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:16.670
and savagely chased Chuck E. around

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:18.350
with the intention of murdering him.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:20.620
Eventually Chuck E. was cornered
and with no nowhere to go,

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:22.680
he just accepted the ferocious blood bath

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:23.860
that was about to ensue.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.760
To calm his nerves in his final moments,

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:28.542
Chuck E. decided to sing
and Pasqually was so shocked

00:04:28.542 --> 00:04:30.737
that he dropped his rolling pin and said,

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:32.600
"A mouse that can sing.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:36.582
My restaurant is a saved, I'm
going to make you a star."

00:04:36.582 --> 00:04:39.610
It's not entirely clear to
me if anthropomorphic rats

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:41.560
are commonplace in the
Chuck E. Cheese canon,

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:43.940
because nobody up to this
point seemed all that shocked

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:45.650
by Charles living at an orphanage,

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:48.130
winning a video game
tournament or paying bus fair.

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:49.850
But I guess Pasqually just really thought

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:51.000
this was something special.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.548
It's also worth noting that Mr. Cheese

00:04:52.548 --> 00:04:54.500
would eventually end up playing in a band

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:58.130
with a performing dog, bird
and whatever this guy is.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:59.480
So take that as you will.

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:01.900
But whatever the case may
be, dollar signs lit up

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:03.060
in Pasqually's eyes.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:04.900
And the two brokered an agreement.

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:06.860
Pasqually would let his
furry little intruder live

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.880
in exchange for free labor.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:11.010
To prepare for the arrival
of the singing mouse,

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.900
Pasqually changed the
name of his restaurant

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:14.020
to Chuck E. Cheese's,

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:16.110
home of the world's famous singing mouse

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:19.070
which was inaccurate considering
he wasn't famous at all yet

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:20.880
because the restaurant had yet to open

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.940
and as I mentioned earlier,
Charles is clearly a rat.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:26.170
On opening night in May 1977,

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:29.040
the place was packed as
Pasqually introduced Chuck E.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.544
Ladies and gentleman,

00:05:30.544 --> 00:05:34.220
please welcome a Chuck E. Cheese. (laughs)

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.490
Okay dude, I can't anymore
with the Italian accent.

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:38.470
However, when it was time to perform

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:39.890
Chuck E. got stage fright.

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:41.490
So the crowd just started booing

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:43.700
because they saw this
rat sitting on a stool

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:44.730
not doing anything.

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:47.170
Understandably, they probably
wanted their money back

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:48.760
and everyone just started leaving.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:50.020
And as they hit the streets,

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:51.850
Charles just watched them out the window.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:54.360
That's when he noticed a
little boy in a birthday crown

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:57.450
and almost instinctively
started singing happy birthday.

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:58.283
At this time,

00:05:58.283 --> 00:06:00.830
the song was owned by the estate
of Mildred and Patty Hill.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:03.090
And Mildred just came outta
the shadows and just 360,

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:05.310
choke slammed the little
Chuck E. with a lawsuit.

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:06.430
Okay, that didn't happen.

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:07.370
But what did happen

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:09.420
was the kid ended up
having his birthday party

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:10.490
at Chuck E. Cheese's.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:12.530
And that's basically what
they became known for.

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:14.420
However, much to Charles chagrin

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.640
that would not become
all they became known for

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:17.870
as the expansion of the chain

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:20.841
led to the coverup of
a slew of dark secrets.

00:06:20.841 --> 00:06:24.674
(dramatic suspenseful music)

00:06:26.402 --> 00:06:29.980
(bright upbeat music)

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:32.330
As Chuck E's restaurant
blew up in popularity,

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:34.070
he would also blow up in size.

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:36.300
Eventually becoming larger
than Pasqually himself,

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.290
gaining a ton of weight and towering over

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:39.740
his young restaurant patrons.

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:41.370
I imagine his obsession with pizza

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:43.520
contributed to his rapid obesification.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:45.560
But this major growth
spurt would not stop him

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:47.690
from doing what he loved, making music.

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:49.740
The popularity of Chuck E. and Pasqually's

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:50.770
musical performances

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:52.630
led them to expand this
part of the business

00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:54.200
by bringing in additional performers

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.760
to form an in restaurant band.

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:58.333
They would call themselves,
The Pizza Time Players.

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:01.123
- Pizza time.

00:07:01.123 --> 00:07:03.770
- And the original lineup
consisted of Chuck E. on vocals,

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:06.507
Pasqually seemingly also a vocalist.

00:07:06.507 --> 00:07:09.620
♪ Halaa, you know I'm
here to make it a pizza ♪

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:12.380
A banjo playing hound,
dog named Jasper T Jowls

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:14.260
and a feline named Crusty the Cat

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:15.860
who didn't seem to have an instrument

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:17.530
other than this baseball bat.

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:19.898
He may have just been there to
intimidate audience members.

00:07:19.898 --> 00:07:21.910
There were also three backup vocalists

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:22.743
known as the Warblettes,

00:07:22.743 --> 00:07:25.550
and the band was often joined
by a female guest performer.

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:27.720
It was at this time that
Chuck E. took up smoking

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:29.500
and it seems that being the front man

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:33.160
or front rat of the band
gave him a considerable ego

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:35.140
as he would often berate
his fellow band mates

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:36.713
while performing on stage.

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:41.540
- That's 'cause it's not
your birthday, nitwit.

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:43.410
Geez folks, I gotta tell you

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:44.900
it's a tough way to make a living

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.187
sitting up here plugged
in to the same computer

00:07:47.187 --> 00:07:48.950
as that (beep) dog.

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:51.140
- This verbal abuse may
have been part of the reason

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:53.760
that Crusty left the band in November 1978

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:55.380
and was replaced by Mr. Munch,

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:58.300
who can only be described as
a horrifying purple monster

00:07:58.300 --> 00:07:59.400
who played the keyboard.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.590
Like Chuck E., Mr. Munch loved pizza.

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:04.113
And I think the two boned. (laughs)

00:08:04.113 --> 00:08:06.110
I accidentally wrote the two boned.

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:08.120
Like Chuck E., Mr. Munch loved pizza

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:10.440
and I think the two
bonded over this passion.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:12.770
They seemed to jive better
than Charles and Crusty did.

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:15.470
Unfortunately it would
appear that Mr. Munch's love

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:17.711
did not stop with pizza.

00:08:17.711 --> 00:08:19.794
♪ You were 16 ♪

00:08:19.794 --> 00:08:20.929
♪ Not seven, but six ♪

00:08:20.929 --> 00:08:22.749
♪ My pizza queen ♪

00:08:22.749 --> 00:08:24.612
♪ Not the king but the queen ♪

00:08:24.612 --> 00:08:25.445
Yike.

00:08:25.445 --> 00:08:27.830
In 1981, Pasqually went
public with the company.

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:28.920
And a couple years later,

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:30.760
Charles would find the
missing piece of the band

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:31.950
that he'd been searching for.

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:34.210
Helen Henny was one of the
previous guest musicians

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:36.080
who cycled into the band in the late 70s.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:38.250
So they brought her on
full time to play guitar.

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:40.600
I'm guessing Pasqually had
some kind of requirement

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:41.870
for all of the other band members

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:44.620
to be some kind of giant
talking animal or monster.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.240
He probably had more faith in the novelty

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:48.590
of giant humanoid creatures
attracting customers

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:50.683
than their actual musical ability.

00:08:52.637 --> 00:08:53.550
(disturbing scream)

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:54.870
Yeah, I can see why.

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:57.870
The lineup of Charles, Pasqually,
Jasper, Munch and Helen

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:00.590
would become the core lineup
for years and years to come.

00:09:00.590 --> 00:09:01.610
There were other characters

00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:03.240
who filled small roles over the years,

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:06.320
like a giant disco singing
skunk named Sally Sashay.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:08.300
A suggestive blues piano playing hippo

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:11.400
named Dolly Dimples and my
personal favorite, Building,

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:13.690
a high rise building who
provided backup vocals

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:15.450
with a horrifying human mouth.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:17.480
The band thrived into the 1980s,

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:19.600
but the company was not
just based on music.

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:20.920
There was also an arcade,

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:22.550
which is one of the main draws for kids

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:25.075
because it allowed them to
partake in legal gambling.

00:09:25.075 --> 00:09:28.039
- Come on, come on, come on, come on.

00:09:28.039 --> 00:09:29.873
Ah, dang it.

00:09:29.873 --> 00:09:32.060
- To this day, I still don't understand

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:34.810
why you have to be 21 years
old to gamble in a casino

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:36.440
where you exchange money for chips

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:38.200
that represent monetary value,

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.820
but children of all ages
can gamble at an arcade

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:42.730
like Chuck E. Cheese or Dave &amp; Busters.

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:44.490
Where you exchange money for tokens

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:46.420
that represent monetary value.

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:48.250
I guess the main difference
is that at a casino,

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:50.930
you can cash your chips
back in for well, cash.

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:52.560
And at Chuck E. Cheese's, you win tickets

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:55.170
that can only be exchanged
for really sh**ty prizes

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:57.340
except for the a disco ball,
that thing was awesome.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:59.550
- I got a blue monster.

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:00.930
- But if the point of a gambling age

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:03.720
is because gambling is recognized
as an addictive behavior

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:06.830
akin to drugs or alcohol,
you're still gambling your money

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:08.410
even if it is in the form of tokens.

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:10.760
So if you're a kid, you're
still wiring your brain

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:11.670
with that behavior.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:13.030
It would be like if they said it was okay

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:14.300
for kids to drink alcohol,

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:16.060
as long as they buy it with tokens.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:18.180
- Chuck E. Cheese, you
know the place where a kid

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:20.020
could be a kid,

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:24.460
the place with a giant rat
that loves pizza and beer.

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:28.930
Imagine that, a kid-friendly
establishment serving beer.

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:31.233
- But anyways, games were a
big part of Chuck E. Cheese's.

00:10:31.233 --> 00:10:34.430
And the 1980s saw gamers
migrating from the arcade

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:35.470
into the living room,

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:37.410
thanks to the popularity of home consoles

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:40.620
like the Atari 2600 and the
Nintendo Entertainment System.

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:42.627
- Zelda!!

00:10:42.627 --> 00:10:44.027
(native battle cry and pig squeal)

00:10:44.027 --> 00:10:46.420
- Which meant you could get
your hands on plenty of high,

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:48.080
but mostly low quality titles

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:49.650
without visiting Chuck E. Cheese,

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:53.100
which was not good news for
this overgrown rat conglomerate.

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:54.790
Chuck and Pasqually were forced to file

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:57.870
for chapter 11 bankruptcy
on March 28th, 1984.

00:10:57.870 --> 00:11:00.262
With losses upward of $15 million.

00:11:00.262 --> 00:11:01.760
- He need the cash.

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:03.371
- Hang in there, Howie.

00:11:03.371 --> 00:11:06.120
- [Zac] The rat was in a trap
and to make matters worse,

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:08.010
they were feeling pressure
from their competitors.

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:10.440
One Chuck E. Cheese imitator
known as Showbiz Pizza

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.280
had their own band of disturbing
humanoid animal performers

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:15.070
known as The Rock-a-fire Explosion.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:17.890
As the sound of the name would
imply, this band was heavier,

00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:19.930
buffer and holy sh*t, who the f*ck thought

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:21.900
it would be a good idea for
these things to entertain

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:23.590
five to 10 year old children?

00:11:23.590 --> 00:11:25.610
Chuck E. and the gang were about to be in

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:27.485
for the fights of their lives.

00:11:28.479 --> 00:11:32.690
(dramatic suspenseful music)

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:35.020
- [Tommy NC] I've been
looking at this honestly.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:38.180
So please tell me that
this is not frightening.

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:41.001
It blinks, it talks, it's a robot.

00:11:41.001 --> 00:11:43.680
But tell me that's not frightening.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:46.680
It may be Chuck E. Cheese,
but that's frightening.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.900
- The early to mid 80s
were a very trying time

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:50.650
for Charles and his band of misfits.

00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:53.240
At one point, they were in
such dire financial straits

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:55.730
that Mr. Munch actually
resorted to eating trash,

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:58.496
a haunting telltale
sign of things to come.

00:11:58.496 --> 00:12:02.845
(jazz music)

00:12:02.845 --> 00:12:03.840
After two difficult years

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:06.350
following the great
video game crash of 1983,

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:08.030
ShowBiz Pizza Time Incorporated

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:10.570
made a deal to purchase Chuck
E. Cheese's Pizza Time Theater

00:12:10.570 --> 00:12:12.290
in May of 1985.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:13.220
Lucky for Chuck E,

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:15.510
he had made a name for himself
over the last eight years.

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:16.930
And despite the failing company,

00:12:16.930 --> 00:12:19.940
was more of an icon than his
arch rival, Billy Bob Brockali,

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:21.830
the front man for The Rockafire Explosion.

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:23.310
So the business decision was made

00:12:23.310 --> 00:12:25.880
to make Charles the face
of the unified franchise.

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:27.498
Now this is just speculation,

00:12:27.498 --> 00:12:30.060
but it seems like Chuck E.
might have been afraid of Billy

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:30.893
and his goons,

00:12:30.893 --> 00:12:32.630
and it's not hard to understand why.

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:34.750
We don't exactly know what
went on behind the scenes

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:35.840
between these two bands

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:38.560
but we do know that Chuck
E's life continued to spiral.

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:40.550
It's speculated that
Charles became a victim

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:42.770
of his own environment and
began to deal with drug

00:12:42.770 --> 00:12:43.850
and alcohol issues.

00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:45.400
It would appear that it got so bad

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:46.935
that he lost control of his own band

00:12:46.935 --> 00:12:49.440
and Mr. Munch became the face of the act.

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:52.793
In 1989, they rebranded to
Munch's Make Believe band.

00:12:53.890 --> 00:12:55.160
Not that make believe.

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:57.220
It was also around this
time that Pasqually

00:12:57.220 --> 00:12:59.510
switched from playing the
accordion to the drums.

00:12:59.510 --> 00:13:00.350
Although it seems like

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:02.917
he may have possibly also
been on drugs as well.

00:13:02.917 --> 00:13:05.500
(upbeat music)

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:10.500
Over the next decade,

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:12.880
Chuck E. Cheese did recover
from the financial strain,

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:15.250
but this would not be without
new new problems arising.

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:17.280
Look at this horrifying
birthday party footage

00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:19.009
from December of 1993.

00:13:19.009 --> 00:13:22.280
(suspenseful music)

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:25.197
(group chattering)

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:28.873
But in reality,

00:13:28.873 --> 00:13:31.830
the '90's and 2000s would be
some of Charles' peak years.

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:34.320
This era is considered the
golden era of the company.

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:36.240
And he even took up
skateboarding as a hobby

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:38.060
and began to lose some weight.

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:38.893
- It is extremely important

00:13:38.893 --> 00:13:42.920
to keep in the best physical
shape possible at all times.

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:43.893
- You got that right.

00:13:43.893 --> 00:13:45.150
- I'm not just saying this

00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:46.770
because this was the era when I was

00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:48.100
of Chuck E. Cheese going age.

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:49.970
Chuck was thriving, healthier than ever,

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:51.070
and on top of everything,

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:52.760
it seems like he was
having a lot of success

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:53.810
with the ladies.

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:56.129
- You can just ask him.

00:13:56.129 --> 00:13:57.250
♪ Chuck yeah! ♪

00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:58.460
- Oh yeah, this is also the time

00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:00.607
when he started using the
catchphrase, Chuck yeah.

00:14:00.607 --> 00:14:02.200
