00:17:49.163 --> 00:17:51.480
(upbeat music)

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:53.300
- And that's enough of that.

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:55.660
If anyone wants to see me do
a Things You Missed episode

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:58.030
on Chuck E. Cheese in the Galaxy 5000,

00:17:58.030 --> 00:18:00.040
I'm gonna need to see like 1000 retweets.

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:01.990
The film ended up being pretty divisive

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:04.240
if the Letterbox rating
is anything to go off of,

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:05.940
but the movie was successful with kids

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:07.980
and served as a part of
Charles' streak of success

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:10.560
to cap off the 90's and take
him into the new millennium.

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:12.110
While there may not
have been many scandals

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:14.080
on the public record
during this time period,

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:16.711
there is reason to believe that
Chuck E.'s actual experiences

00:18:16.711 --> 00:18:18.770
during this so-called golden age

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:21.512
were not as clean as previously believed.

00:18:21.512 --> 00:18:25.345
(dramatic suspenseful music)

00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:31.660
Earlier in this lesson,

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:33.370
I mentioned what appeared from the outside

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:35.440
to be drug and gambling
addictions for Charles

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:36.320
in the late '80s.

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:38.530
And it's my impression
that these personal issues

00:18:38.530 --> 00:18:39.450
never went away,

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:40.870
but rather that Chuck E

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:42.930
and the ever expanding
corporation behind him

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:44.270
got better at covering them up

00:18:44.270 --> 00:18:46.000
