00:19:58.820 --> 00:19:59.900
- [Man] You're Chuck E, ain't you?

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:00.733
Oh, look at him.

00:20:00.733 --> 00:20:01.680
- [Woman] They were celebrating

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:02.970
their two year old son's birthday

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:05.470
when they were hauled out of
Chuck E. Cheese's in handcuffs.

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:07.058
He says it all started
because of a long line

00:20:07.058 --> 00:20:08.420
at the photo booth.

00:20:08.420 --> 00:20:10.170
- [Man] Police released
this surveillance video

00:20:10.170 --> 00:20:11.730
from a Chuck E. Cheese restaurant.

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:14.072
- [Woman] These are live pictures
over the Chuck E. Cheese.

00:20:14.072 --> 00:20:17.072
(suspenseful music)

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:20.780
- [Man] Being held on
charges of indecent exposure

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:22.756
after two incidents at
the Chuck E. Cheese.

00:20:22.756 --> 00:20:23.589
- Aw,

00:20:23.589 --> 00:20:25.106
(child crying)

00:20:25.106 --> 00:20:26.422
all on tape too.

00:20:26.422 --> 00:20:28.651
(suspenseful music)

00:20:28.651 --> 00:20:31.511
One little girl's crushed hope, priceless.

00:20:31.511 --> 00:20:33.850
♪ Chuck E., Chuck E ♪

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:36.060
- Seems like this could
have just been talked out,

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:37.865
but instead it went outta control.

00:20:37.865 --> 00:20:41.384
- I don't wanna go to
Chuck E. Cheese no more.

00:20:41.384 --> 00:20:42.784
(suspenseful music)

00:20:42.784 --> 00:20:44.350
(horror music)

00:20:44.350 --> 00:20:47.170
- Tonight we take a look
at a disturbing phenomenon.

00:20:47.170 --> 00:20:49.420
- [Man] Type Chuck E. Cheese into YouTube

00:20:49.420 --> 00:20:51.428
and multiple fights unfold.

00:20:51.428 --> 00:20:52.261
- GET BACK OVER THERE!

00:20:52.261 --> 00:20:54.230
- We had about an 18 month period

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:56.135
where we were there 17 times.

00:20:56.135 --> 00:20:57.840
- And the videos are lighting up YouTube.

00:20:57.840 --> 00:21:00.690
- [Man] They charged eight
people with disorderly conduct.

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:04.240
- The three year old left all
alone when Chuck E. Cheese-

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:05.334
(screams of agony)

00:21:05.334 --> 00:21:06.413
- [Woman] And they're here.

00:21:06.413 --> 00:21:08.009
- [Man] Oh no!

00:21:08.009 --> 00:21:09.820
- [Chuck E] Oh, yeah!

00:21:09.820 --> 00:21:11.840
- Entertainment center for
children is shutting down.

00:21:11.840 --> 00:21:13.420
- Argument between two women.

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:14.860
One of them pulled out a handgun.

00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:16.530
- [Woman] A child actually found a baggie

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:17.826
with a white substance.

00:21:17.826 --> 00:21:18.659
(scream)

00:21:18.659 --> 00:21:20.400
- [Woman] Birthday party
turned into a brawl.

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:22.200
- The birthday boy's
grandmother was trampled.

00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:24.540
- [Woman] It was ugly and violent.

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:26.223
- Birthday brawl at a Chuck E.

00:21:26.223 --> 00:21:28.106
(horror music and screams)

00:21:28.106 --> 00:21:29.380
(group chattering)

00:21:29.380 --> 00:21:32.150
- [Man] Anything that wasn't
bolted to the floor was used.

00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:33.500
- Two men arrested at Chuck E.

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:34.893
(horror music)

00:21:36.410 --> 00:21:38.265
- [Woman] Gunfire, shattered window.

00:21:38.265 --> 00:21:39.098
(screams of agony)

00:21:40.045 --> 00:21:40.905
- Oh!

00:21:40.905 --> 00:21:43.078
(group chattering)

00:21:43.078 --> 00:21:44.430
- [Man] Several injured people here.

00:21:44.430 --> 00:21:46.335
- [Man] Slam dunk, go!

00:21:46.335 --> 00:21:47.340
- Slam dunk.

00:21:47.340 --> 00:21:48.907
- [Man] First taken the Chuck E. Cheese.

00:21:48.907 --> 00:21:53.224
(dramatic suspenseful music)

00:21:53.224 --> 00:21:57.249
(multiple news reports overlayed)

00:22:02.927 --> 00:22:06.760
(high pitched ringing)

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:11.970
- [Zac] With each and every
misstep being magnified

00:22:11.970 --> 00:22:13.420
and going viral on the internet,

00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:15.820
Charles Entertainment
Cheese was feeling pressure

00:22:15.820 --> 00:22:18.470
from all directions and
retreated from the public eye

00:22:18.470 --> 00:22:21.230
replacing himself with a
younger, thinner mouse character

00:22:21.230 --> 00:22:22.820
hoping that kids would not notice

00:22:22.820 --> 00:22:24.600
that this was not the real Charles,

00:22:24.600 --> 00:22:27.040
much like what happened
to Jake from State Farm.

00:22:27.040 --> 00:22:28.940
But there was one YouTube scandal

00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:33.840
that would rise far, far above
any that had come before it.

00:22:33.840 --> 00:22:38.590
(musterious music)

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:47.500
- Hi there, I just got an idea
how to make Chuck E. Cheese's

00:22:47.500 --> 00:22:50.420
better than ever: brand new pizza!

00:22:50.420 --> 00:22:52.210
Genius, if I do say so myself.

00:22:52.210 --> 00:22:55.580
- So I have a theory that
I have wanted to talk about

00:22:55.580 --> 00:22:56.500
for a long time.

00:22:56.500 --> 00:22:58.890
- [Zac] OG YouTube creator, Shane Dawson

00:22:58.890 --> 00:23:01.090
and known for his exaggerated
character portrayals

00:23:01.090 --> 00:23:02.240
in the early days of the site

00:23:02.240 --> 00:23:04.720
had pretty much moved on
from short films and vlogs

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:07.060
to longer documentary style content.

00:23:07.060 --> 00:23:09.690
In 2018, Shane was one of
the most popular creators

00:23:09.690 --> 00:23:10.523
on the platform

00:23:10.523 --> 00:23:12.370
and seemed to have the
Internet's full attention

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:14.090
whenever he released a new video.

00:23:14.090 --> 00:23:16.180
On February 11th 2019,

00:23:16.180 --> 00:23:19.270
Shane released the second in
his two-part Conspiracy Series,

00:23:19.270 --> 00:23:20.285
where he investigated a rumor

00:23:20.285 --> 00:23:21.900
that Chuck E. Cheese restaurants

00:23:21.900 --> 00:23:24.200
collect and re-use uneaten pizzas.

00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:25.033
The rumor derived

00:23:25.033 --> 00:23:27.120
from the appearance of
Chuck E. Cheese pizzas.

00:23:27.120 --> 00:23:29.850
Oftentimes the slices didn't
match up with their neighbors,

00:23:29.850 --> 00:23:31.050
were not the right size

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:33.530
and sometimes didn't
even form a full pizza.

00:23:33.530 --> 00:23:35.320
Shane decided to go to a nearby restaurant

00:23:35.320 --> 00:23:37.560
to see for himself and he
was shocked to discover

00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:39.410
that his pizza was as disjointed

00:23:39.410 --> 00:23:41.200
as the ones he had seen on the internet.

00:23:41.200 --> 00:23:43.300
He tried to reverse
engineer the pie at home

00:23:43.300 --> 00:23:44.879
and came to the conclusion that his pizza

00:23:44.879 --> 00:23:47.940
was an amalgamation of multiple pizzas.

00:23:47.940 --> 00:23:49.360
- [Pasqually] Good luck.

00:23:49.360 --> 00:23:52.931
And remember the proof is in the crust.

00:23:52.931 --> 00:23:54.471
- [Man] That's a Chuck E.
Cheese pizza right there.

00:23:54.471 --> 00:23:55.554
Look at this.

00:23:58.150 --> 00:24:01.407
- Mystery still unsolved.

00:24:01.407 --> 00:24:05.070
- The uproar that this video
caused was unbelievable.

00:24:05.070 --> 00:24:07.440
This video was only the very beginning

00:24:07.440 --> 00:24:10.320
of the worst two years that
this northeast dwelling rodent

00:24:10.320 --> 00:24:12.358
would ever endure.

00:24:12.358 --> 00:24:15.358
(suspenseful music)

00:24:17.142 --> 00:24:19.642
(mysterious music)

00:24:20.873 --> 00:24:23.030
After the release of
Investigating Conspiracies

00:24:23.030 --> 00:24:23.940
with Shane Dawson,

00:24:23.940 --> 00:24:26.400
the topic immediately trended
on Twitter and YouTube

00:24:26.400 --> 00:24:28.110
with some of the biggest
creators on the site

00:24:28.110 --> 00:24:29.270
covering the topic.

00:24:29.270 --> 00:24:32.470
- Shane Dawson seemingly ruined
pizza for a lot of people

00:24:32.470 --> 00:24:34.560
so much so to the point
that Chuck E. Cheese

00:24:34.560 --> 00:24:36.060
even had to release a statement.

00:24:36.060 --> 00:24:38.420
- [Keemstar] Each pizza is handmade,

00:24:38.420 --> 00:24:41.143
which means the amount of
sauce and cheese and toppings

00:24:41.143 --> 00:24:44.400
might vary, but it still tastes great.

00:24:44.400 --> 00:24:46.773
- The real conspiracy is not the pizza.

00:24:46.773 --> 00:24:49.965
The real conspiracy theory is what the-

00:24:49.965 --> 00:24:50.798
(censor)

00:24:50.798 --> 00:24:51.829
is with these mascots?

00:24:51.829 --> 00:24:52.662
(woman laughing)

00:24:52.662 --> 00:24:54.470
- Even though this controversy
is about the pizza,

00:24:54.470 --> 00:24:56.120
which Charles Entertainment Cheese

00:24:56.120 --> 00:24:58.110
has literally no hand in the creation of

00:24:58.110 --> 00:24:59.870
despite the claims of
this Tampa Bay news group,

00:24:59.870 --> 00:25:01.330
people were still finding a way

00:25:01.330 --> 00:25:03.350
to drag the company's beloved mascot.

00:25:03.350 --> 00:25:06.020
Which again, had already
been replaced by this younger

00:25:06.020 --> 00:25:07.330
and more kid friendly mouse

00:25:07.330 --> 00:25:10.230
who is also instructed to
respond to the name Chuck E.

00:25:10.230 --> 00:25:12.400
I'm pretty sure the purpose
of this was to get Charles,

00:25:12.400 --> 00:25:14.640
who was getting older,
he was now approaching 50

00:25:14.640 --> 00:25:16.920
away from the kids because
as you may have noticed,

00:25:16.920 --> 00:25:19.300
he was getting pretty
creepy as most people do

00:25:19.300 --> 00:25:20.133
when they age.

00:25:20.133 --> 00:25:25.064
- Change da world, my
final message, goodbye.

00:25:27.755 --> 00:25:32.755
(Windows 95 startup sound)

00:25:33.422 --> 00:25:34.940
- However, the new Chuck E,

00:25:34.940 --> 00:25:36.420
I'll just call him Chuck E. Jr.

00:25:36.420 --> 00:25:38.400
despite the fact that
he's clearly not related

00:25:38.400 --> 00:25:40.960
to our original Chuck E.,
who is a rat, not a mouse

00:25:40.960 --> 00:25:43.550
had only taken over
seven years prior in 2012

00:25:43.550 --> 00:25:45.340
and was already starting
to take the mantle

00:25:45.340 --> 00:25:47.167
of deranged overgrown rodent.

00:25:47.167 --> 00:25:50.167
(suspenseful music)

00:25:52.370 --> 00:25:56.190
Oh my God, nothing says
comfortable eating establishment

00:25:56.190 --> 00:25:57.908
like those eyes just
surveying the restaurant

00:25:57.908 --> 00:25:59.030
for their next prey.

00:25:59.030 --> 00:26:00.680
Maybe if they had this in the restaurant

00:26:00.680 --> 00:26:01.900
from the demon child video,

00:26:01.900 --> 00:26:03.940
he would have actually
been scared into behaving.

00:26:03.940 --> 00:26:06.750
In addition to big channels
making videos about this topic,

00:26:06.750 --> 00:26:09.070
you also had an entire
industry of creators

00:26:09.070 --> 00:26:10.250
popping up overnight,

00:26:10.250 --> 00:26:11.450
where they would claim to be current

00:26:11.450 --> 00:26:13.020
or former Chuck E. Cheese employees

00:26:13.020 --> 00:26:14.730
and expose these so-called truth

00:26:14.730 --> 00:26:16.310
about the pizza controversy.

00:26:16.310 --> 00:26:18.690
I'm sure the fact that they
are all millennial women

00:26:18.690 --> 00:26:21.620
who look like they want
attention is a total coincidence.

00:26:21.620 --> 00:26:23.550
Shane Dawson really did a number

00:26:23.550 --> 00:26:25.410
on CEC Entertainment's bottom line,

00:26:25.410 --> 00:26:27.260
which I just realized that
the name of the company

00:26:27.260 --> 00:26:28.093
literally stands

00:26:28.093 --> 00:26:30.380
for Charles Entertainment
Cheese Entertainment.

00:26:30.380 --> 00:26:32.090
I'm like, why do you have to
have the word entertainment

00:26:32.090 --> 00:26:32.923
in there twice?

00:26:32.923 --> 00:26:34.910
There is one more thing
that I wanna highlight

00:26:34.910 --> 00:26:36.330
about the company's response.

00:26:36.330 --> 00:26:37.510
When I saw Shane's video,

00:26:37.510 --> 00:26:40.220
I assumed that they did combine
pizzas of different types,

00:26:40.220 --> 00:26:42.160
but it was probably all
done in the kitchen.

00:26:42.160 --> 00:26:44.300
They were not collecting
pizzas from the dining room

00:26:44.300 --> 00:26:45.230
and reheating them.

00:26:45.230 --> 00:26:47.380
So essentially if someone
orders half cheese,

00:26:47.380 --> 00:26:49.420
half pepperoni and another table orders

00:26:49.420 --> 00:26:50.660
half cheese, half mushroom,

00:26:50.660 --> 00:26:52.970
they might split one
full cheese pizza in half

00:26:52.970 --> 00:26:54.610
to use as the two cheese halves.

00:26:54.610 --> 00:26:56.700
If there are a lot of orders
going on at the same time

00:26:56.700 --> 00:26:57.533
during rush hour,

00:26:57.533 --> 00:26:58.880
this might be the most efficient way

00:26:58.880 --> 00:27:01.050
to serve as many fresh pizzas as possible.

00:27:01.050 --> 00:27:03.170
The same could be said
about singles slices.

00:27:03.170 --> 00:27:05.040
If a pizza consists of eight slices

00:27:05.040 --> 00:27:07.020
and seven people order a single slice,

00:27:07.020 --> 00:27:09.220
they could make use of
that last remaining slice

00:27:09.220 --> 00:27:11.660
by adding it to another
pizza before it goes bad.

00:27:11.660 --> 00:27:13.240
And there's nothing wrong with doing that.

00:27:13.240 --> 00:27:14.980
However in their response,

00:27:14.980 --> 00:27:16.450
they don't try to claim that at all.

00:27:16.450 --> 00:27:18.990
They just start going off about
how the pizzas are handmade

00:27:18.990 --> 00:27:21.230
and they're made in house
so they aren't uniform,

00:27:21.230 --> 00:27:23.210
which literally doesn't
address the main concerns

00:27:23.210 --> 00:27:25.040
that Shane brought up in his video at all.

00:27:25.040 --> 00:27:26.320
- Why are you the only pizza place

00:27:26.320 --> 00:27:29.820
that has non-uniform pizzas,
just doesn't really make sense.

00:27:29.820 --> 00:27:31.660
- Excellent point, Shira Lazar.

00:27:31.660 --> 00:27:34.360
Allegedly they also sent Shane
a cease and desist notice.

00:27:34.360 --> 00:27:36.040
And in true horror movie fashion,

00:27:36.040 --> 00:27:39.538
Shane even began to fear for his own life.

00:27:39.538 --> 00:27:42.190
- There's things about
this video that actually

00:27:42.190 --> 00:27:45.337
I have to worry about like getting killed.

00:27:45.337 --> 00:27:49.430
- Whoa, I guess maybe Pasqually
has some mafia connections.

00:27:49.430 --> 00:27:51.620
- That cash ought to be slashing my fund

00:27:51.620 --> 00:27:53.100
and kicks in my back.

00:27:53.100 --> 00:27:55.590
- MatPat in an episode of
his show, "Food Theory"

00:27:55.590 --> 00:27:58.450
did a big investigation
into Chuck E. Cheese Pizzas.

00:27:58.450 --> 00:28:00.470
(suspenseful music)

00:28:00.470 --> 00:28:01.490
- [Man] This isn't about the fact

00:28:01.490 --> 00:28:03.630
that Chuck E. Cheese pizzas
aren't perfectly round,

00:28:03.630 --> 00:28:05.687
it's that pizzas don't look cohesive

00:28:05.687 --> 00:28:09.698
like every other pizza in existence does.

00:28:09.698 --> 00:28:11.610
All you guys had to do was say,

00:28:11.610 --> 00:28:15.530
we do not recycle other consumers' pizza.

00:28:15.530 --> 00:28:17.700
And you didn't do that!

00:28:17.700 --> 00:28:19.540
- MatPat essentially did disprove

00:28:19.540 --> 00:28:20.750
the recycled pizzas theory

00:28:20.750 --> 00:28:22.260
by ordering Chuck E. Cheese pizzas

00:28:22.260 --> 00:28:24.360
during the COVID-19 restrictions in 2020

00:28:24.360 --> 00:28:25.880
when in restaurant dining was closed

00:28:25.880 --> 00:28:27.770
and still getting disjointed pizzas.

00:28:27.770 --> 00:28:31.120
However, this could have been
4D chess by chef Pasqually.

00:28:31.120 --> 00:28:33.270
Maybe he was intentionally
making uneven pizzas

00:28:33.270 --> 00:28:34.950
during the pandemic to convince people

00:28:34.950 --> 00:28:37.040
that that's just how
their pizzas always look.

00:28:37.040 --> 00:28:39.340
MatPat talked to a
supposed current employee

00:28:39.340 --> 00:28:40.490
at Chuck E. Cheese who claimed

00:28:40.490 --> 00:28:42.100
that the blade that
they used to cut pizzas

00:28:42.100 --> 00:28:44.560
is essentially very dull because
Chuck E. Cheese employees

00:28:44.560 --> 00:28:46.870
couldn't be trusted with
sharp objects apparently.

00:28:46.870 --> 00:28:48.340
So they have to apply more force,

00:28:48.340 --> 00:28:49.760
which stretches out the pizza.

00:28:49.760 --> 00:28:52.150
He also claims that the
mismatched pepperoni slices

00:28:52.150 --> 00:28:54.580
probably just slipped under
the crust as a result of this.

00:28:54.580 --> 00:28:56.530
MatPat was satisfied with this conclusion.

00:28:56.530 --> 00:28:58.478
However, it doesn't answer
one of the mysteries

00:28:58.478 --> 00:28:59.880
from Shane's video.

00:28:59.880 --> 00:29:01.360
In the pizza that Shane received,

00:29:01.360 --> 00:29:03.770
one of the slices didn't go
all the way through the pizza

00:29:03.770 --> 00:29:04.900
as you would expect.

00:29:04.900 --> 00:29:06.340
So three years later,

00:29:06.340 --> 00:29:08.450
I still don't feel like we
have a satisfying answer

00:29:08.450 --> 00:29:09.283
to this mystery.

00:29:09.283 --> 00:29:11.450
After recovering from
bankruptcy in the '80s,

00:29:11.450 --> 00:29:13.770
Chuck E. came back and
survived an array of punches

00:29:13.770 --> 00:29:16.370
from various news outlets
and one big punch to the head

00:29:16.370 --> 00:29:18.671
from one of YouTube's biggest juggernauts.

00:29:18.671 --> 00:29:22.495
- [Woman] Are you serious? (crying)

00:29:22.495 --> 00:29:23.328
(scream)

00:29:23.328 --> 00:29:24.310
(distorted audio)

00:29:24.310 --> 00:29:26.730
- But the next big hit would
once again leave Charles

00:29:26.730 --> 00:29:28.760
and his gang of oversized animal musicians

00:29:28.760 --> 00:29:30.970
down for the count.

00:29:30.970 --> 00:29:33.620
- A dangerous virus is
spreading rapidly in China

00:29:33.620 --> 00:29:36.160
and US officials are very
worried that it could come here.

00:29:36.160 --> 00:29:38.230
- A Washington state resident fell ill

00:29:38.230 --> 00:29:40.310
after returning from Wuhan, China.

00:29:40.310 --> 00:29:41.190
- Breaking news tonight,

00:29:41.190 --> 00:29:43.710
the coronavirus forcing
millions more Americans

00:29:43.710 --> 00:29:45.680
into virtual lockdown.

00:29:45.680 --> 00:29:47.290
- [Man] It's eerily silent.

00:29:47.290 --> 00:29:51.040
(dramatic suspenseful music)

00:29:54.047 --> 00:29:57.440
(lo-fi chill music)

00:29:57.440 --> 00:29:58.870
- [Zac] In December 2019,

00:29:58.870 --> 00:30:01.670
a deadly viral outbreak
occurred in Wuhan, China

00:30:01.670 --> 00:30:03.850
and officials were unable
to contain its spread.

00:30:03.850 --> 00:30:05.430
By March 13th, 2020,

00:30:05.430 --> 00:30:07.730
the United States declared
a state of emergency.

00:30:07.730 --> 00:30:09.700
Restaurants and many
other indoor businesses

00:30:09.700 --> 00:30:11.110
were forced to close their doors.

00:30:11.110 --> 00:30:12.940
Some restaurants were able to get by,

00:30:12.940 --> 00:30:15.340
by switching their business
model to focus on delivery

00:30:15.340 --> 00:30:16.500
and curbside pickup.

00:30:16.500 --> 00:30:19.000
Pasqually and Chuck E. were not so lucky.

00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:19.833
Let's face it.

00:30:19.833 --> 00:30:21.480
Nobody was coming to Chuck E. Cheese's

00:30:21.480 --> 00:30:22.740
because they liked the food,

00:30:22.740 --> 00:30:24.950
it was always about the
games and entertainment.

00:30:24.950 --> 00:30:27.100
It was a good birthday party
of destination for kids

00:30:27.100 --> 00:30:28.650
dating back to that first rendition

00:30:28.650 --> 00:30:30.670
of "Happy Birthday" in 1977.

00:30:30.670 --> 00:30:32.180
But with in-person get togethers

00:30:32.180 --> 00:30:33.890
suddenly becoming a safety hazard,

00:30:33.890 --> 00:30:36.800
sending pizzas out was now
their only stream of revenue.

00:30:36.800 --> 00:30:37.840
And fresh off the heels

00:30:37.840 --> 00:30:40.420
of the recycled pizza conspiracy
theory the year before,

00:30:40.420 --> 00:30:42.750
nobody was rushing to their
delivery app of choice

00:30:42.750 --> 00:30:44.490
to order a Chuck E. Cheese pizza.

00:30:44.490 --> 00:30:47.960
The company was dying and Chuck
E, that is the real Chuck E.

00:30:47.960 --> 00:30:49.350
was still nowhere to be seen,

00:30:49.350 --> 00:30:50.950
with Chuck E. Jr still appearing

00:30:50.950 --> 00:30:53.330
in what limited advertisements
were running at the time.

00:30:53.330 --> 00:30:56.860
On June 25th, 2020, parent
company CEC Entertainment

00:30:56.860 --> 00:30:58.660
once again, filed for bankruptcy.

00:30:58.660 --> 00:31:01.600
The next day, the company
announced 34 restaurant closures,

00:31:01.600 --> 00:31:03.905
which was very upsetting
into its clientele.

00:31:03.905 --> 00:31:04.807
- [Man] What?

00:31:04.807 --> 00:31:05.757
- [Boy] It's closed.

00:31:05.757 --> 00:31:09.300
- Not fair! NOT FAIIRRR!!

00:31:09.300 --> 00:31:10.810
- At this point, the real Chuck E.

00:31:10.810 --> 00:31:12.690
has been out of the public eye for years,

00:31:12.690 --> 00:31:14.750
but he still had one thing to hold onto.

00:31:14.750 --> 00:31:16.790
The restaurant was still named after him.

00:31:16.790 --> 00:31:19.640
Many of the locations still
had his image on the sign.

00:31:19.640 --> 00:31:20.660
He had been dragged through

00:31:20.660 --> 00:31:23.090
an almost unbelievable amount of bad PR,

00:31:23.090 --> 00:31:25.800
but Chuck E. was still the
face of Chuck E. Cheese's.

00:31:25.800 --> 00:31:27.550
That would all change.

00:31:27.550 --> 00:31:29.987
The year 2020 saw the
fall of many, many things,

00:31:29.987 --> 00:31:33.840
including the permanent closure
of 17% of all restaurants

00:31:33.840 --> 00:31:36.290
but it also saw the
rise of ghost kitchens.

00:31:36.290 --> 00:31:37.427
What are ghost kitchens?

00:31:37.427 --> 00:31:38.720
In simplest terms,

00:31:38.720 --> 00:31:40.340
a ghost kitchen is a commercial kitchen

00:31:40.340 --> 00:31:41.808
that prepares meals for
a virtual restaurant

00:31:41.808 --> 00:31:44.400
and a virtual restaurant is a restaurant

00:31:44.400 --> 00:31:45.830
with no physical storefront.

00:31:45.830 --> 00:31:47.680
AKA it's delivery only.

00:31:47.680 --> 00:31:49.950
Thanks to the boom in app
based delivery services,

00:31:49.950 --> 00:31:52.340
ghost kitchens exploded
in the pandemic era.

00:31:52.340 --> 00:31:54.720
Most virtual kitchens pay
an existing restaurant

00:31:54.720 --> 00:31:56.310
to use their kitchen as a ghost kitchen,

00:31:56.310 --> 00:31:57.950
or share a physical ghost kitchen

00:31:57.950 --> 00:31:59.370
with other virtual restaurants.

00:31:59.370 --> 00:32:02.080
So restaurants most known for
their dining-in experience,

00:32:02.080 --> 00:32:04.660
whose sales were slumping during
this time of delivery only

00:32:04.660 --> 00:32:07.020
could serve as a ghost
kitchen for another brand.

00:32:07.020 --> 00:32:09.047
How does this all tie
into Chuck E. Cheese?

00:32:09.047 --> 00:32:11.290
Not too many people
looking to order a pizza

00:32:11.290 --> 00:32:12.510
are gonna go with Chuck E. Cheese.

00:32:12.510 --> 00:32:15.020
So Pasqually quietly
introduced a new brand

00:32:15.020 --> 00:32:17.600
and called it Pasqually's Pizza and Wings.

00:32:17.600 --> 00:32:19.360
Pasqually's offers Italian style fare,

00:32:19.360 --> 00:32:20.800
marketed more towards adults

00:32:20.800 --> 00:32:23.180
and used Chuck E. Cheese
restaurants as a ghost kitchen.

00:32:23.180 --> 00:32:24.985
Most adults probably
aren't going to recognize

00:32:24.985 --> 00:32:27.560
the name Pasqually from
their childhood days

00:32:27.560 --> 00:32:30.150
of watching him perform in
Munch's Make Believe Band

00:32:30.150 --> 00:32:31.290
or for the older adults,

00:32:31.290 --> 00:32:32.630
The Pizza Time Players.

00:32:32.630 --> 00:32:35.390
However, it wasn't supposed
to be a highly guarded secret.

00:32:35.390 --> 00:32:37.260
I mean, if you look at
the Pasqually's website,

00:32:37.260 --> 00:32:40.250
it clearly says, brought to
you by CEC Entertainment.

00:32:40.250 --> 00:32:42.380
You're just not gonna
see any mouse or rat logo

00:32:42.380 --> 00:32:43.990
associated with Pasqually's.

00:32:43.990 --> 00:32:46.470
Somehow this also turned
into a controversy,

00:32:46.470 --> 00:32:48.130
even though there's nothing morally wrong

00:32:48.130 --> 00:32:49.090
with them doing this.

00:32:49.090 --> 00:32:51.230
It's honestly just good
marketing and other chains

00:32:51.230 --> 00:32:52.820
like Hooters and Denny's are doing it too

00:32:52.820 --> 00:32:54.560
and nobody had a problem with that.

00:32:54.560 --> 00:32:55.393
Chuck E. Cheese

00:32:55.393 --> 00:32:56.890
actually had to release
a statement about it,

00:32:56.890 --> 00:32:59.210
where they said Pasqually's
Pizza and Wings recipes

00:32:59.210 --> 00:33:01.880
use fresh homemade pizza dough
just like Chuck E. Cheese,

00:33:01.880 --> 00:33:04.370
but it is a different pizza
that features a thicker crust,

00:33:04.370 --> 00:33:06.890
extra sauce and new blends
of cheeses and seasonings,

00:33:06.890 --> 00:33:08.840
giving consumers a more flavorful,

00:33:08.840 --> 00:33:10.490
more premium pizza experience.

00:33:10.490 --> 00:33:12.652
So over the past 43 years

00:33:12.652 --> 00:33:14.910
of Charles involvement with Pasqually.

00:33:14.910 --> 00:33:16.057
- [Pasqually] Were weren't
gay, just for you to know.

00:33:16.057 --> 00:33:18.110
He has as a girlfriend, okay?

00:33:18.110 --> 00:33:19.500
I don't want this to sound gay.

00:33:19.500 --> 00:33:20.730
Am I sounding gay?

00:33:20.730 --> 00:33:22.330
- Over the past 43 years

00:33:22.330 --> 00:33:24.040
of Charles involvement with Pasqually,

00:33:24.040 --> 00:33:26.260
he had gone from being the literal savior

00:33:26.260 --> 00:33:28.890
and new mascot and figurehead
of Pasqually's Pizza

00:33:28.890 --> 00:33:31.060
or as it would become
known: Chuck E. Cheese,

00:33:31.060 --> 00:33:33.670
to being removed from all
marketing and promotional material

00:33:33.670 --> 00:33:36.130
and the name Pasqually's
Pizza being brought back

00:33:36.130 --> 00:33:38.110
as the primary seller
for the parent company,

00:33:38.110 --> 00:33:39.690
because nobody wanted a pie

00:33:39.690 --> 00:33:41.610
associated with an overgrown rat

00:33:41.610 --> 00:33:44.460
unless child gambling
could somehow be involved.

00:33:44.460 --> 00:33:46.820
Is this the end of the once powerful rat

00:33:46.820 --> 00:33:49.170
known as Charles Entertainment Cheese?

00:33:49.170 --> 00:33:52.333
Has Chuck E's time in the
spotlight finally expired?

00:33:53.220 --> 00:33:54.053
Maybe.

00:33:54.053 --> 00:33:56.140
As more restaurants
still continue to reopen

00:33:56.140 --> 00:33:57.940
in 2021 and 2022

00:33:57.940 --> 00:34:00.770
thanks to the rollout of COVID
19 vaccines for children,

00:34:00.770 --> 00:34:02.410
patrons have noticed something missing

00:34:02.410 --> 00:34:04.190
from many Chuck E. Cheese locations.

00:34:04.190 --> 00:34:06.990
The stage that once played
host to talented musicians

00:34:06.990 --> 00:34:10.760
like Helen Henny, Jasper Jowls,
Pasqually Pieplate, Mr.Munch

00:34:10.760 --> 00:34:12.680
and Chuck E. Cheese were now gone

00:34:12.680 --> 00:34:15.590
in place of a light up dance
floor and some TV screens.

00:34:15.590 --> 00:34:17.910
Clearly this is an
outrage and another reason

00:34:17.910 --> 00:34:20.360
the "reject modernity,
embrace tradition" mindset

00:34:20.360 --> 00:34:22.120
is important for our culture.

00:34:22.120 --> 00:34:23.980
But for Charles Entertainment Cheese,

00:34:23.980 --> 00:34:27.780
it may be the erasure of the
last remnants of a by gone era.

00:34:27.780 --> 00:34:30.950
We may have reached an age
where guests are no longer happy

00:34:30.950 --> 00:34:34.110
with Chuck E. Cheese
being in Chuck E. Cheese.

00:34:34.110 --> 00:34:36.550
- [Man] Remember every guest leaves happy

00:34:36.550 --> 00:34:38.673
and our guests always come first.

00:34:41.430 --> 00:34:43.720
- If you enjoyed this
episode of "Horror History,"

00:34:43.720 --> 00:34:44.980
check out that video on the left

00:34:44.980 --> 00:34:47.210
to see me cover the
history of Belle Delphine.

00:34:47.210 --> 00:34:48.930
And if you're confused about why

00:34:48.930 --> 00:34:50.950
I covered big pizza's biggest rodent,

00:34:50.950 --> 00:34:52.500
check out the date of this upload.

00:34:52.500 --> 00:34:54.278
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld World

00:34:54.278 --> 00:34:56.330
for new horrors every week.

00:34:56.330 --> 00:34:58.810
Ring the death bell for all notifications,

00:34:58.810 --> 00:35:01.360
and I will see you in the next one

00:35:01.360 --> 00:35:04.235
assuming we both survive.

